# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Install to /etc/radar/analyst.env (root-owned, 0640, group guardian).
#
#   sudo install -m 0640 -o root -g guardian analyst.env.example /etc/radar/analyst.env
#
# Everything here is deny-by-default. An empty file gives you a service that
# runs, reads nothing, posts nothing, and says so on every tick -- which is the
# resting state, not a broken one.

# Where the reply log, the cursor and the spend ledger live. The unit grants
# write access to this path and to nothing else.
RADAR_ANALYST_DIR=/home/guardian/radar/data/analyst

# --- The credential ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# BOTH or NEITHER. A token with no user id has nothing to poll and a user id
# with no token cannot poll it, so a half-configured instance is treated as
# unconfigured: the publisher falls back to the dry run and nothing is posted.
#
# THIS IS THE SWITCH THAT MAKES THE ACCOUNT PUBLIC. Until both are set, the
# service is a dry run that writes replies to the log and shows them to nobody.
#
# RADAR_X_BEARER=
# RADAR_X_USER_ID=

# --- Prices ------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ALL FOUR or the service answers nothing. There are no defaults, and that is
# deliberate: a default price is a spending decision made by whoever wrote the
# code, and this repository has an ADR's worth of regret about deciding on an
# unverified number.
#
# Micro-USD, whole numbers, so a price is written exactly:
#
#   $0.001 =  1000        $0.005 =  5000
#   $0.010 = 10000        $0.200 = 200000
#
# Two of these are not yet verified against a real invoice and are the reason
# this file asks rather than assumes: whether a mentions poll bills as an owned
# read ($0.001) or a standard one ($0.005), and whether a summoned reply
# carrying a URL is $0.010 or $0.200. Put in what you were actually charged.
#
# RADAR_X_PRICE_MENTION_READ=1000
# RADAR_X_PRICE_POST_READ=5000
# RADAR_X_PRICE_REPLY=10000
# RADAR_MODEL_PER_CALL_USD_MICRO=2000

# --- The ceiling -------------------------------------------------------------
#
# BOTH or the budget is CLOSED and every call is refused. In dollars, because an
# operator writing a daily cap thinks in dollars. A value that will not parse is
# also closed: a typo in a spending ceiling must not read as permission.
#
# RADAR_ANALYST_DAILY_USD=5.00
# RADAR_ANALYST_PER_CALL_USD=0.25

# --- Who gets answered -------------------------------------------------------
#
# Unset means ZERO, and zero means refuse. These are what stop one account
# emptying the day's budget, and what stop the same coin being answered twice.
#
# RADAR_ANALYST_PER_SUMMONER_DAILY=3
# RADAR_ANALYST_GLOBAL_DAILY=50
# RADAR_ANALYST_DEDUPE_SECONDS=3600

# --- The chain ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The RPC endpoint the dossier is read from. Direct, never the x402 lane: a
# mention is answered into a live thread and on-chain settlement adds hundreds
# of milliseconds before a response returns (AGENTS.md rule 7).
#
# RADAR_RPC_URL=

# --- The voice ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Optional. Without it every reply is the deterministic template, which is a
# working product rather than a degraded one -- it just has no jokes in it.
#
# Note the model must be the metered API path, never the subscription CLI: that
# one is marked private use only, and this account is public.
#
# RADAR_MODEL_API_KEY=
# RADAR_MODEL_ENDPOINT=https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages
# RADAR_MODEL_NAME=
# RADAR_MODEL_PRICE_IN=
# RADAR_MODEL_PRICE_OUT=
